# Force LF checkout for all text files regardless of the runner's git
# core.autocrlf setting. GitHub-hosted windows-latest runners default to
# core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites every tracked text file (README.md,
# AGENTS.npm.md, test fixtures, source) to CRLF on checkout. Several
# regexes across the test suite hardcode a literal "\n" (e.g. matching
# ```typescript\n code fences), which then fail to match at all under
# CRLF, and any test that compares checked-out fixture content byte-for-
# byte against freshly-generated (LF) output mismatches purely on line
# endings - neither is a real cross-platform behavior difference.
* text=auto eol=lf

vendor/cpython-emscripten/python.wasm filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
